Package: memlkit
Type: Package
Title: Unified Mixed-Effects Tree Models for Panel and Multilevel Data
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: person("Iron", "Hong", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), email = "righttocity123@gmail.com")
Description: Provides unified interfaces for longitudinal panel data and
    cross-sectional multilevel data. Supports mixed-effects random forests,
    mixed-effects gradient boosting, and LightGBM extensions for regression
    and classification. Panel gradient boosting follows Olaniran et al. (2025)
    <doi:10.1038/s41598-025-16526-z>; longitudinal random forests follow
    Capitaine et al. (2021) <doi:10.1177/0962280220946080> and Hajjem et al.
    (2014) <doi:10.1080/00949655.2012.741599>. The multilevel mixed-effects
    random forest workflow follows Krennmair and Schmid (2022)
    <doi:10.1111/rssc.12600>. Includes prediction, random-effect extraction,
    variable importance, partial dependence plots, and model comparison.
